  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "If $y=|x-5|$, what are the coordinates of the minimum point on the graph?",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that $y=|x-a|$ is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $a$ units right.\n\nThe function $y=|x-5|$ has $a=5.$ Therefore, it is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $5$ units right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250789/assets/ca70d305bb0da32441611d879ca2a4a2453b38e951b448964b5d48f01fa33e28.png)\n\nLooking at the graph, we can see that the coordinates of the minimum point are $(5,0).$",
